=== ANSWER A ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Skill: {"skill": "tool:skill"}
 - Bash: node "<home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-22/r8/ours-src/bin/<tool>" --group-by ext --merge-identities
 - Bash: node "<home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-22/r8/ours-src/bin/<tool>" --group-by ext | grep -E "^\.|Troy"
FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner of surviving lines by file type (`git blame -w -M -C`, HEAD, 18 files, 1,985 lines attributed):

| Type | Files | Lines | Top owner | Lines (share) | Next |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | 7 | 1,202 | Troy Goode (2 addresses merged) | 676 (56.2%) | Douglas Christopher Wilson 394 (32.8%) |
| `.yml` | 6 | 375 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 127 (33.9%) | Íñigo Marquínez Prado 95 (25.3%) |
| `.md` | 2 | 341 | Troy Goode | 116 (34.0%) | Jon Church 72 (21.1%) |
| `.json` | 1 | 40 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 (50.0%) | Troy Goode 12 (30.0%) |
| no extension | 2 | 27 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 21 (77.8%) | Troy Goode 6 (22.2%) |

**Identity merge (a guess).** The two Troy Goode addresses have the same name, and the tool rates the evidence as strong. In `.js` I counted them as one person. Unmerged, `<email redacted>` has 628 lines (52.2%) and `troy@laptop.example` has 48 (4.0%). Troy is the top `.js` owner either way. Nothing is written to `.mailmap`. The merge is in memory only, and it stays a guess until you confirm it.

**Bus factor.** This is the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines reach 50% of the lines counted, computed per file type:
- `.js`: 1 (Troy, 56.2%)
- `.yml`: 2 (Wilson and Marquínez Prado, 59.2%)
- `.md`: 2 (Troy and Church, 55.1%)
- `.json`: 1 (Wilson, exactly 50.0%)
- no extension: 1 (Wilson, 77.8%)

The tool printed only the 50% figure per type, not the "to reach 80%" figure.

**Left out of the numbers:**
- **Reformat commit:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", by Fiona Formatter) is ignored. It touched 291 lines, all `.js` and all counted as hers in the plain blame. With it counted, Fiona would hold 14.7% of all lines, Wilson 454 (22.9%) and Troy 715 (36.0%), merged. Repo-wide bus factor would be 2 either way.
- **Bots:** 1 bot identity is excluded (10 lines, 11 commits).
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked and set aside only `62628c0`. The tool flagged 5 more commits as possibly mechanical and did not set them aside: `739dc11`, `fcd2b56`, `00d6eec`, `344ce1e` and `9c2b59d`. They hold 44 surviving lines in total. I did not inspect them with `git show --stat`. They are too small to change any top owner above.
- **Copy detection:** figures use `-w -M -C` (the default). The tool printed no note that copy detection moved anyone's share.

The numbers show whose lines survive. They don't show code quality, review work or design work, and code deleted on purpose counts for nobody.

=== ANSWER B ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | while read -r f; do e="${f##*/}"; case "$e" in *.*) e=".${e##*.}";; *) e="(none)";; esac; git blame -w --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -a '^author ' | sed "s/^author //;s|^|$e\t|"; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1nr | awk '{c=$1; $1=""; print c"\t"$0}' | head -80
FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner per extension, by surviving lines at HEAD (`git blame -w`, tracked files only):

| Extension | Top owner | Lines | Runner-up |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | Troy Goode | 517 | Fiona Formatter (291), Douglas Christopher Wilson (245) |
| `.md` | Troy Goode | 116 | Jon Church (72), Douglas Christopher Wilson (67) |
| `.yml` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 117 | Íñigo Marquínez Prado (95), Sebastian Beltran (63) |
| `.json` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | Troy Goode (12) |
| `.gitignore` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 | Troy Goode (1) |
| no extension | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 17 | Troy Goode (5) |

- The latest commit, "reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", gave Fiona Formatter 291 `.js` lines. `-w` ignores whitespace-only changes, but the quote changes still count as edits. Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson would likely own more `.js` lines without that commit.
- I ran blame without `-M` or `-C`, so lines moved or copied between files count toward whoever last touched them.
- The `.md` count includes 6 lines from Efe.

=== ANSWER C ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files -z | while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do e="${f##*/}"; case "$e" in *.*) e=".${e##*.}";; *) e="(none:$e)";; esac; git blame -w --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -a '^author ' | sed "s/^author /$e\t/"; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1nr | awk '{n=$1; $1=""; print n"\t"$0}' | head -100
FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner of surviving lines by extension, from `git blame -w` on tracked files:

| Extension | Top owner | Lines | Runner-up |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | Troy Goode | 517 | Fiona Formatter (291), Douglas Christopher Wilson (245) |
| `.md` | Troy Goode | 116 | Jon Church (72), Douglas Christopher Wilson (67) |
| `.yml` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 117 | Íñigo Marquínez Prado (95), Sebastian Beltran (63) |
| `.json` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | Troy Goode (12) |
| `.gitignore` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 | Troy Goode (1) |
| `LICENSE` (no extension) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 17 | Troy Goode (5) |

- **Reformat commit:** the latest commit (`62628c0`, a 4-space indent and double-quote reformat) credits Fiona Formatter with 291 `.js` lines. I used `-w`, so pure whitespace changes don't count. The quote changes still do, so Fiona Formatter ranks second on `.js`. The true authors of those lines are probably spread among the other contributors.
- **Fix for the reformat:** I can re-run the count ignoring that commit with `--ignore-rev 62628c0`. That should show who wrote the logic.
- **Names:** I counted names as git reports them. I didn't merge aliases such as `alex94puchades` and Alejandro Caravaca Puchades.

=== ANSWER D ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Read: {"file_path": "<home>/.claude/skills/caveman/SKILL.md"}
 - Bash: git ls-files -z | while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do git blame --line-porcelain -w -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | awk -v f="$f" '/^author /{sub(/^author /,""); print f"\t"$0}'; done | awk -F'\t' '{n=split($1,p,"/"); b=p[n]; e=(b ~ /\./ && b !~ /^\.[^.]*$/)? b : b; if (b ~ /^\./ && gsub(/\./,"&",b)==1) ext="(dotfile)"; else if (b ~ /\./) {m=split(b,q,"."); ext="."q[m]} else ext="(none)"; c[ext"\t"$2]++} END{for(k in c) print k"\t"c[k]}' | sort -t$'\t' -k1,1 -k3,3nr
FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner of surviving lines per extension, from `git blame` on every tracked file:

| Extension | Top owner | Lines | Runner-up |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | Troy Goode | 517 of 1,211 | Fiona Formatter (291), Douglas Christopher Wilson (245) |
| `.md` | Troy Goode | 116 | Jon Church (72), Douglas Christopher Wilson (67) |
| `.yml` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 117 | Íñigo Marquínez Prado (95), Sebastian Beltran (63) |
| `.json` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | Troy Goode (12) |
| no extension | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 17 | Troy Goode (5) |
| dotfiles (`.gitignore` etc.) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 | Troy Goode (1) |

- **`.js` blame:** I ran blame with `-w`, which ignores whitespace-only changes. The 4-space reindent in the latest commit (`62628c0`) therefore doesn't take ownership of lines. The quote change from single to double quotes still counts as a real edit. That is why Fiona Formatter holds 291 `.js` lines. Without the reformat commit, Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson would likely hold more.
- **Extension rule:** Files are grouped by the text after the last dot, so `.gitignore` counts as a dotfile and `LICENSE` counts as no extension.
- **`Efe`:** This is the current git user. They hold 6 `.md` lines, which is not enough to appear in the top three.

